# TDD The Right Way

### Project Installation
After downloading the project, run:
- composer install

### Database Setup
Start a database using one of these options:
- Docker: run `docker compose up -d` (a Postgres container; stop it with `docker compose down`)
- Your own database: set up your database credentials in the `.env.test.local` file

Then run:
- symfony console doctrine:database:create -e test
- symfony console doctrine:schema:create -e test
- symfony run bin/phpunit (you should see "No tests executed!")

### Workshop Requirements
- PHP 8.4 or greater
- Environment ready to run a traditional Symfony app
- Any database compatible with Doctrine

### Nice to have:
- Ability to run tests through your IDE
